      "description": "Current Blender facts. Directory query={mode:directory} with include_image=false returns tight evaluated world bounds, AABB centers and an independent directory binding. Task set example: {\"include_image\":false,\"query\":{\"mode\":\"task\",\"target\":{\"name\":\"A\"},\"candidates\":[{\"name\":\"B\"}],\"requested_facts\":[\"closed_solid_relation\",\"surface_proximity\"]}}. Opt in to spatial_relation and surface_proximity for support-certified separation with closed-classification fallback. Unknown/duplicate rows remain. Complete penetration/nearest-separated sets require all relevant evidence; otherwise only known subsets are reported. Legacy objects pair/aabb supported. Global surface_nearest instead uses one query.objects selector without focal_id, or focal_id with query={\"mode\":\"surface_nearest\"}; session_id and include_image=false required. Complete means global nearest; partial means best-known. scene_revision/fingerprint bind this capture/source/revision; runtime_source_sha256 identifies code. Scene edits expire observations. Goals are caller criteria. For all current scene mesh pairs use query={\"mode\":\"surface_scan\",\"threshold_m\":0.002}. This text-only scan includes hidden meshes, needs no selectors, includes threshold equality and reports coverage. Its unsigned triangle-surface distance describes surface proximity. Solid relations require separate facts. For surface_scan, omitted response_detail or brief returns a versioned compact table with readable names, object-table references, original distance_m and derived distance_mm. Explicit full returns detailed current evidence with witnesses. Combine observations using their scene/source binding.",
